  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_adv.reading.structure-cohesion",
   "title_zh": "看懂文章結構與連接詞的功能（text structure & cohesion）",
   "can_do": "我能看出一段文章是用比較對照、因果、時序還是問題-解決來組織，也能說出 however、therefore、for example 這類連接詞在句子裡的功能。",
   "situation_group": "閱讀：篇章結構與連貫",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "reading",
   "est_minutes": 10,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_adv.reading.text-structure",
    "eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_mid.reading.main-detail"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-text-structure-types", "text": "Writers organize a text in a pattern. Common patterns are: time order (what happens first, next, last), compare-and-contrast (how two things are alike or different), cause-and-effect (why something happens and what results), and problem-and-solution. The pattern that fits most of the sentences is the main structure.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "作者會用某種模式組織文章：時序（先、再、最後）、比較對照（兩件事怎麼像／怎麼不同）、因果（為什麼發生、結果如何）、問題-解決；對得上多數句子的那個模式才是主要結構；屬英語閱讀教學通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-cohesion-connectors", "text": "Linking words join ideas and show their relationship. 'However' signals a contrast (the opposite). 'Therefore' signals a result or conclusion (so). 'For example' signals an example. Knowing a connector's job helps you follow the writer's thinking.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "連接詞把想法接起來並顯示它們的關係：however＝轉折／相反，therefore＝結果／結論（所以），for example＝舉例；知道連接詞的功能有助於跟上作者的思路；屬英語語法／閱讀通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.text-structure"],
     "body": "Writers do not put sentences in random order. They use a pattern. Four common patterns are: time order (events from first to last), compare-and-contrast (how two things are alike or different), cause-and-effect (a reason and its result), and problem-and-solution. To name the structure, ask which pattern fits most of the sentences, not just the last line.",
     "zh_hint": "作者不會把句子亂排，而是用某種模式。四種常見模式：時序（事件由先到後）、比較對照（兩件事怎麼像或不同）、因果（原因和它的結果）、問題-解決。判斷結構時，問『哪個模式對得上大多數句子』，而不是只看最後一句。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"],
     "body": "Linking words act like road signs between ideas. 'However' and 'but' mean a contrast is coming — the opposite of what was just said. 'Therefore' and 'so' mean a result or conclusion. 'For example' means an example will follow. When you see one, it tells you how the next idea connects to the one before.",
     "zh_hint": "連接詞像想法之間的路標。however、but 代表接下來是『轉折／相反』——跟剛剛說的相反；therefore、so 代表『結果／結論』；for example 代表後面要『舉例』。看到它，就知道下一個想法跟前面怎麼接起來。"},
    {"kind": "passage", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.text-structure", "eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"],
     "body": "Cats and dogs are both popular pets, but they are quite different. Dogs are active and need daily walks outside. Cats, however, are happy to stay indoors and sleep for many hours. Dogs often want to play with people, while cats enjoy time alone. Therefore, people who are very busy may find a cat easier to keep.",
     "zh_hint": "導讀：這段在講貓和狗。先看出整段主要用什麼方式組織（它一直在把貓和狗拿來比）；再注意 however、while、therefore 這些連接詞在句子裡各是什麼功能。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.text-structure", "eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"],
     "body": "Structure: almost every sentence puts a dog fact next to a cat fact ('but they are quite different', 'however', 'while'), so the main structure is compare-and-contrast. Cohesion: 'however' signals a contrast — cats are the opposite of active dogs. 'Therefore' at the end signals a conclusion drawn from the contrast.",
     "zh_hint": "結構：幾乎每句都把狗的事和貓的事擺在一起比（but they are quite different、however、while），所以主要結構是『比較對照』。連貫：however 代表轉折——貓和好動的狗相反；最後的 therefore 代表由前面的對比得出的結論。"}
   ],

   "practice": [
    {"question_id": "R6-structure", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "這段短文主要是用什麼方式來組織內容？", "answer": "比較對照（把貓和狗的異同拿來對比）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.text-structure"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.text-structure"],
     "options": ["比較對照（把貓和狗的異同拿來對比）", "依時間先後排列事件", "問題與解決的結構", "按步驟說明怎麼養寵物"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "依時間先後排列事件": "文中沒有『先…再…最後』的時間順序，而是一直在對比兩種動物。",
      "問題與解決的結構": "文中沒有先提出一個問題再給解法；它是在比較貓和狗。",
      "按步驟說明怎麼養寵物": "文中沒有一步步教養寵物的做法。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-text-structure-types"],
     "feedback": "全段幾乎每句都把狗和貓擺在一起比（different、however、while），所以主要結構是『比較對照』；最後的 therefore 只是結尾下的小結論，不是全文結構。"},

    {"question_id": "R6-cohesion-however", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "文中 'Cats, however, are happy to stay indoors' 裡的 however，功能是什麼？", "answer": "表示轉折、相反（貓和前面的狗相反）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"],
     "options": ["表示轉折、相反（貓和前面的狗相反）", "表示原因", "表示舉例", "表示時間先後"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "表示原因": "however 不是用來給原因；給原因的是 because 這類字。",
      "表示舉例": "舉例會用 for example；however 不是舉例。",
      "表示時間先後": "however 不表示時間順序；表時間會用 first、then、after。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-cohesion-connectors"],
     "feedback": "前一句說狗好動要外出，however 接著說貓剛好相反、愛待在室內——so however 的功能是『轉折／相反』。"},

    {"question_id": "R6-cohesion-therefore", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "文中最後 'Therefore, people who are very busy may find a cat easier to keep' 裡的 Therefore，功能是什麼？", "answer": "表示結果、結論（所以）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cohesion"],
     "options": ["表示結果、結論（所以）", "表示相反、轉折", "表示舉一個例子", "表示再補充一個相同的點"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "表示相反、轉折": "表相反會用 however、but；therefore 不是轉折。",
      "表示舉一個例子": "舉例用 for example；therefore 不是舉例。",
      "表示再補充一個相同的點": "再補充會用 also、in addition；therefore 是由前面推出的結論。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-cohesion-connectors"],
     "feedback": "作者先比較了貓和狗，therefore 接著用這個對比得出結論『所以很忙的人養貓比較輕鬆』——so therefore 的功能是『結果／結論』。"}
   ],

   "selfeval": ["還不熟", "快會了", "會了"],
   "selfeval_note": "翻看答案自己判斷（不自動判讀）；選完進入 SRS 間隔複習。",

   "shadowing": {
    "note": "朗讀練習（不產音檔、不自動判讀）：出聲讀這兩句，讀到 however、therefore 時停一下，想想它在句子裡的功能（相反？結論？）。",
    "lines": [
     {"text": "Cats, however, are happy to stay indoors and sleep for many hours."},
     {"text": "Therefore, people who are very busy may find a cat easier to keep."}
    ]
   }
  },

  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_adv.reading.factopinion-graph",
   "title_zh": "分辨事實與意見、判讀簡單數據（fact vs opinion & graph integration）",
   "can_do": "我能分辨一句話是可查證的事實還是個人的意見，也能讀懂用文字描述的簡單數據，找出最大、最小或算出合計。",
   "situation_group": "閱讀：事實與意見、數據判讀",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "reading",
   "est_minutes": 10,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_adv.reading.fact-vs-opinion",
    "eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_mid.reading.main-detail"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-fact-vs-opinion", "text": "A fact is something that can be checked and shown to be true or false, such as a number or a date. An opinion is what someone feels or believes, which can differ from person to person. Signal words like 'I think', 'the best', and 'should' often mark an opinion.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "事實＝可以查證、能判定真假的事（如數字、日期）；意見＝某人的感受或看法，因人而異；I think、the best、should 這類字常標示出意見；屬英語閱讀教學通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-graph-integration", "text": "Data can be given in words, like 'Group A read 12 books'. To answer a data question, read each number carefully, then compare them (which is the most or least) or combine them (add two groups together). The numbers in the text are the only evidence you need.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "數據可以用文字給出，如『Group A read 12 books』；回答數據題時，仔細讀每個數字，再做比較（誰最多／最少）或合計（把兩組相加）；文中的數字就是你唯一需要的依據；屬英語閱讀教學通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.fact-vs-opinion"],
     "body": "A fact can be checked and proven true or false. 'The library has 500 books' is a fact — you can count them. An opinion is what a person feels or believes; it can change from person to person. 'Reading is the best hobby' is an opinion — not everyone agrees. Signal words such as 'I think', 'the best', 'beautiful', and 'should' often point to an opinion.",
     "zh_hint": "事實可以查證、能判定真假。'The library has 500 books' 是事實——可以數。意見是某人的感受或看法，因人而異。'Reading is the best hobby' 是意見——不是人人都同意。I think、the best、beautiful、should 這類字常指向意見。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"],
     "body": "Numbers are sometimes written inside the text instead of drawn in a chart. Read each number with care. Then do what the question asks: find the largest or smallest, or add two numbers together. Everything you need is in the words — do not guess beyond the numbers given.",
     "zh_hint": "數字有時寫在文字裡，而不是畫成圖。仔細讀每一個數字，再照題目要的去做：找最大或最小，或把兩個數字相加。你需要的全都在文字裡——不要超出給的數字去猜。"},
    {"kind": "passage", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.fact-vs-opinion", "eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"],
     "body": "Our class counted how many books each group read last month. Group A read 12 books. Group B read 8 books. Group C read 15 books. So Group C read the most. I think reading is the best hobby of all, and everyone should read more books.",
     "zh_hint": "導讀：這段先給三組讀書的數據（A 12、B 8、C 15），再講作者的看法。一邊讀一邊分：哪些句子是『可查證的事實』（數字），哪一句是『作者的意見』；數據題則回到數字去比較或相加。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.fact-vs-opinion", "eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"],
     "body": "Fact or opinion: 'Group A read 12 books' is a fact — you can check the count. 'I think reading is the best hobby of all' is an opinion — it uses 'I think' and 'the best', and not everyone agrees. Data: the three numbers are 12, 8, and 15, so Group C (15) read the most, and Group A and B together read 12 + 8 = 20 books.",
     "zh_hint": "事實或意見：'Group A read 12 books' 是事實——數字可查；'I think reading is the best hobby of all' 是意見——用了 I think、the best，而且不是人人同意。數據：三個數字是 12、8、15，所以 C 組（15）讀最多；A 組加 B 組共 12 + 8 = 20 本。"}
   ],

   "practice": [
    {"question_id": "R7-opinion", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "下列哪一句是作者的『意見』，而不是事實？", "answer": "I think reading is the best hobby of all.（我認為閱讀是最棒的嗜好）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.fact-vs-opinion"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.fact-vs-opinion"],
     "options": ["I think reading is the best hobby of all.（我認為閱讀是最棒的嗜好）", "Group A read 12 books.（A 組讀了 12 本書）", "Group C read 15 books.（C 組讀了 15 本書）", "Group C read the most.（C 組讀最多）"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "Group A read 12 books.（A 組讀了 12 本書）": "這是可以數、可以查證的數字，是事實。",
      "Group C read 15 books.（C 組讀了 15 本書）": "這也是可查證的數字，是事實。",
      "Group C read the most.（C 組讀最多）": "由 12、8、15 可以驗證 C 最多，這是能判定真假的事實。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-fact-vs-opinion"],
     "feedback": "'I think... the best hobby of all' 用了 I think、the best，是作者的看法、因人而異，所以是意見；其他三句都是可查證的數字或由數字得出的事實。"},

    {"question_id": "R7-graph-most", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "根據這段數據，哪一組讀的書最多？", "answer": "C 組（15 本）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"],
     "options": ["C 組（15 本）", "A 組（12 本）", "B 組（8 本）", "三組讀的一樣多"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "A 組（12 本）": "A 組是 12 本，比 C 組的 15 本少。",
      "B 組（8 本）": "B 組只有 8 本，是三組裡最少的。",
      "三組讀的一樣多": "三組是 12、8、15，數字不同，不是一樣多。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-graph-integration"],
     "feedback": "三組分別是 A 12、B 8、C 15；15 最大，所以 C 組讀最多。"},

    {"question_id": "R7-graph-sum", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "A 組和 B 組合起來，一共讀了幾本書？", "answer": "20 本",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.graph-integration"],
     "options": ["20 本", "23 本", "27 本", "15 本"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "23 本": "23 是 A（12）加 C（15）的結果，不是 A 加 B。",
      "27 本": "27 是 B（8）加 C（15）＋4 之類的誤算；A 加 B 應是 12＋8。",
      "15 本": "15 是 C 組一組的數字，不是 A 加 B 的合計。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-graph-integration"],
     "feedback": "A 組 12 本加 B 組 8 本，12 ＋ 8 ＝ 20 本。"}
   ],

   "selfeval": ["還不熟", "快會了", "會了"],
   "selfeval_note": "翻看答案自己判斷（不自動判讀）；選完進入 SRS 間隔複習。",

   "shadowing": {
    "note": "朗讀練習（不產音檔、不自動判讀）：出聲讀這兩句，讀第一句時確認它是『可查證的數字（事實）』，讀第二句時注意 I think、the best 這種『意見』的訊號字。",
    "lines": [
     {"text": "Group A read 12 books, and Group C read 15 books."},
     {"text": "I think reading is the best hobby of all."}
    ]
   }
  },

  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_adv.reading.multitext-ordering",
   "title_zh": "跨兩篇短文整合資訊與把句子排成合理順序（multi-text & ordering）",
   "can_do": "我能把兩篇短文的資訊合起來回答問題，也能把打散的句子依時間詞和連接詞排成唯一合理的順序。",
   "situation_group": "閱讀：多文本整合與排序",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "reading",
   "est_minutes": 10,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text",
    "eng.t_adv.reading.discourse-ordering"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_mid.reading.main-detail", "eng.t_adv.reading.title-purpose"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-multi-text", "text": "Sometimes the answer is not in one text alone. You must take a piece of information from Text A and a piece from Text B and put them together. First find what each text gives, then combine them to answer.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "有時答案不在單獨一篇裡；你要從 Text A 取一個資訊、從 Text B 取一個資訊，再把它們合起來。先找出每篇各給了什麼，再整合來回答；屬英語閱讀教學通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-discourse-ordering", "text": "To put scrambled sentences in order, use the signal words. Words like 'First', 'Then', 'After...', and 'Finally' lock the sequence, because each one must come at its own place in time. Follow the clues to find the one order that makes sense.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "要把打散的句子排好，就用訊號字；First、Then、After…、Finally 這些字會鎖定順序，因為每個都必須落在它自己的時間位置；跟著線索就能找出唯一說得通的順序；屬英語閱讀教學通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text"],
     "body": "Some questions cannot be answered from one text alone. You may need a price from one notice and a plan from a message. The trick is to read both texts first, note what each one tells you, and then put the two pieces together. The answer lives in the two texts combined, not in either one by itself.",
     "zh_hint": "有些問題沒辦法只看一篇就答出來。你可能要從一張告示拿到價格，再從一則訊息拿到計畫。訣竅是：先讀兩篇，記下每篇告訴你什麼，再把兩塊資訊合起來。答案在『兩篇合起來』裡，不在單獨任何一篇。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.discourse-ordering"],
     "body": "When sentences are mixed up, signal words show the right order. 'First' marks the beginning. 'Then' and 'After...' mark the middle steps, in the order the clues allow. 'Finally' marks the end. Use these words to lock each sentence into its one correct place.",
     "zh_hint": "當句子被打散時，訊號字會指出正確順序。First 標示開頭；Then、After… 標示中間的步驟（依線索允許的順序）；Finally 標示結尾。用這些字把每一句鎖進它唯一正確的位置。"},
    {"kind": "passage", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text", "eng.t_adv.reading.discourse-ordering"],
     "body": "Text A (a notice): SCHOOL BOOK SALE. Saturday, 9:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. Storybooks cost 20 dollars each. Comic books cost 30 dollars each. Text B (a message): Lily wants to buy two storybooks and one comic book. She has 80 dollars.",
     "zh_hint": "導讀：Text A 是賣書告示（故事書每本 20、漫畫每本 30），Text B 是訊息（莉莉想買兩本故事書和一本漫畫，她有 80 元）。有些問題要把兩篇合起來才答得出（價格在 A、她要買什麼和有多少錢在 B）。另外也練習把打散的句子排順序。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text", "eng.t_adv.reading.discourse-ordering"],
     "body": "Multi-text: from Text A, storybooks are 20 and comics are 30. From Text B, Lily wants two storybooks and one comic. Combine them: 20 + 20 + 30 = 70 dollars. Since she has 80, she will have 80 - 70 = 10 dollars left. Ordering: for the sentences 'First, I put a tea bag in a cup', 'Then I poured hot water', 'After three minutes, I took it out', 'Finally, I drank the tea', the signal words give one order: First, Then, After, Finally.",
     "zh_hint": "多文本整合：由 Text A 知道故事書 20、漫畫 30；由 Text B 知道莉莉要兩本故事書加一本漫畫。合起來：20 ＋ 20 ＋ 30 ＝ 70 元。她有 80，所以還剩 80 － 70 ＝ 10 元。排序：像 First…、Then…、After three minutes…、Finally… 這組句子，訊號字給出唯一順序：First → Then → After → Finally。"}
   ],

   "practice": [
    {"question_id": "R8-multitext-total", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "把兩篇合起來看：莉莉想買的東西（兩本故事書、一本漫畫）一共要花多少錢？", "answer": "70 元",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text"],
     "options": ["70 元", "50 元", "80 元", "90 元"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "50 元": "50 像是只算一本故事書加一本漫畫（20＋30），少算了一本故事書。",
      "80 元": "80 是莉莉『有』的錢（Text B），不是她要花的金額。",
      "90 元": "90 像是把漫畫算成兩本（20＋30＋30＋10）之類的誤算；她只買一本漫畫。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-multi-text"],
     "feedback": "價格在 Text A（故事書 20、漫畫 30），數量在 Text B（兩本故事書、一本漫畫）：20 ＋ 20 ＋ 30 ＝ 70 元。"},

    {"question_id": "R8-multitext-left", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "莉莉用她的錢買完這些書後，還會剩下多少錢？", "answer": "10 元",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.multi-text"],
     "options": ["10 元", "20 元", "70 元", "不夠錢，不能全買"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "20 元": "20 像是少算了一本書的誤差；要花的是 70，剩的是 80－70。",
      "70 元": "70 是她要花的錢，不是剩下的錢。",
      "不夠錢，不能全買": "她有 80 元，要花 70 元，夠買，還會剩錢。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-multi-text"],
     "feedback": "她要花 70 元（上一題），手上有 80 元（Text B），所以剩 80 － 70 ＝ 10 元。"},

    {"question_id": "R8-ordering", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "下面四句話被打散了，依照句子裡的訊號字，正確的先後順序是哪一個？（(1) Finally, I added honey and drank the tea.　(2) First, I put a tea bag into a cup.　(3) After three minutes, I took the tea bag out.　(4) Then I poured hot water into the cup.）", "answer": "(2) → (4) → (3) → (1)",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.discourse-ordering"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.discourse-ordering"],
     "options": ["(2) → (4) → (3) → (1)", "(2) → (3) → (4) → (1)", "(1) → (2) → (4) → (3)", "(2) → (4) → (1) → (3)"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "(2) → (3) → (4) → (1)": "這把 'After three minutes, I took the tea bag out' 排在倒水之前；但要先倒熱水（Then）泡著，才可能三分鐘後把茶包拿出來，順序顛倒。",
      "(1) → (2) → (4) → (3)": "這把 Finally（最後）排到最前面，但 Finally 明明是結尾，不可能最先。",
      "(2) → (4) → (1) → (3)": "這把 Finally（喝茶）排在『拿出茶包』之前；但 Finally 是最後一步，應排最後。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-discourse-ordering"],
     "feedback": "訊號字鎖定順序：First（2）先放茶包 → Then（4）倒熱水 → After three minutes（3）拿出茶包 → Finally（1）加蜂蜜喝茶，所以是 (2)→(4)→(3)→(1)。"}
   ],

   "selfeval": ["還不熟", "快會了", "會了"],
   "selfeval_note": "翻看答案自己判斷（不自動判讀）；選完進入 SRS 間隔複習。",

   "shadowing": {
    "note": "朗讀練習（不產音檔、不自動判讀）：出聲讀這兩句（泡茶步驟的頭尾），讀的時候注意 First、Finally 這些訊號字怎麼把順序鎖定。",
    "lines": [
     {"text": "First, I put a tea bag into a cup."},
     {"text": "Finally, I added some honey and drank the tea."}
    ]
   }
  },

  {
   "unit_id": "eng.t_adv.reading.cloze-gap",
   "title_zh": "綜合克漏字與句子選填（cloze & gap filling）",
   "can_do": "我能依語意和語法，在句中空格選出最適合的字，也能在段落的空格選出最適合填入的句子。",
   "situation_group": "閱讀：克漏字與選填",
   "subject": "eng",
   "strand": "reading",
   "est_minutes": 10,
   "knowledge_point_ids": [
    "eng.t_adv.reading.cloze",
    "eng.t_adv.reading.gap-filling"
   ],
   "prerequisites": ["eng.t_mid.reading.main-detail"],
   "reuse_pages": [],

   "claims": [
    {"claim_id": "c-cloze-meaning-grammar", "text": "In a cloze, you choose the best word for a blank. The right word must fit both the meaning (it makes sense with the sentence) and the grammar (the correct form, such as the right verb tense or subject agreement). Check both before you choose.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "克漏字是要為空格選最適合的字；正確的字必須語意說得通、語法也對（正確的形式，如時態或主詞一致）；選之前兩個都要檢查；屬英語閱讀教學通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"},
    {"claim_id": "c-gap-filling-sentence", "text": "In sentence gap-filling, you choose the sentence that best fits a blank in a paragraph. The right sentence connects smoothly to the sentence before and after, and stays on the same topic. A sentence that is off-topic or contradicts the text does not fit.",
     "kind": "language-usage", "source_refs": ["Cambridge English"],
     "verification_ref": "句子選填是要為段落的空格選最適合填入的句子；正確的句子要和前後句自然接得上、而且維持同一主題；離題或和文意相反的句子不合適；屬英語閱讀教學通則；待英語母語 reviewer 複核", "risk_class": "normal", "status": "provisional"}
   ],

   "teach": [
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cloze"],
     "body": "A cloze has blanks inside a passage. For each blank, choose the one word that fits best. Two tests must both pass. The meaning test: does the word make sense here? The grammar test: is it the right form — the right tense, or the right verb to match the subject? A word can sound close but still be wrong if it fails either test.",
     "zh_hint": "克漏字在短文裡留空格。每個空格選最適合的一個字。要同時通過兩個檢查。語意檢查：這個字在這裡說得通嗎？語法檢查：形式對不對——時態對嗎、動詞和主詞一致嗎？一個字聽起來很接近，但只要有一項沒過，就還是錯的。"},
    {"kind": "text", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.gap-filling"],
     "body": "In sentence gap-filling, a whole sentence is missing from a paragraph. Choose the sentence that fits the blank best. Read the sentence before and the sentence after the blank. The right choice links them smoothly and keeps the same topic. A sentence that jumps to a new topic, or says the opposite of the text, does not belong.",
     "zh_hint": "句子選填是段落裡少了一整句。選最適合填進空格的句子。先讀空格前一句和後一句；正確的選項要能把它們順順地接起來、並維持同一主題。跳到新主題、或和文意相反的句子，都不該放進去。"},
    {"kind": "passage", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cloze", "eng.t_adv.reading.gap-filling"],
     "body": "Plants need a few things to grow well. Water comes first. A plant (1)___ water every day to stay alive. Plants also need sunlight, because sunlight (2)___ them make their food. In addition, the soil must be good. (3)___ With water, sunlight, and good soil, a plant can grow strong and green.",
     "zh_hint": "導讀：這段在講植物生長需要的東西，裡面有空格。(1)、(2) 是『克漏字』——依語意和語法選最適合的『字』；(3) 是『句子選填』——選最適合接在這裡的『句子』。填好後整段要讀起來通順、不離題。"},
    {"kind": "example", "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cloze", "eng.t_adv.reading.gap-filling"],
     "body": "Blank (1): the subject is 'A plant' (one plant), so the verb must be 'needs' — 'A plant needs water'. Blank (2): the subject is 'sunlight' (singular) and the passage is in the present, so 'helps' fits — 'sunlight helps them make their food'. Blank (3): the next line lists water, sunlight, and good soil, so the missing sentence should be about soil — 'Good soil holds the roots and gives the plant food' fits best.",
     "zh_hint": "空格 (1)：主詞是 'A plant'（一株植物），動詞要用 'needs'——A plant needs water。空格 (2)：主詞是 'sunlight'（單數），整段是現在式，所以用 'helps'——sunlight helps them make their food。空格 (3)：下一句列出水、陽光和好土壤，所以少的句子應該講土壤——'Good soil holds the roots and gives the plant food.' 最合適。"}
   ],

   "practice": [
    {"question_id": "R9-cloze-1", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "空格 (1)：'A plant ___ water every day to stay alive.' 最適合填入哪個字？", "answer": "needs",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cloze"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cloze"],
     "options": ["needs", "need", "needing", "to need"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "need": "主詞是單數的 'A plant'，動詞要用第三人稱單數 needs；need 用於複數主詞（如 Plants need）。",
      "needing": "needing 是 -ing 形，不能單獨當這句的主要動詞（需要 is／are 等助動詞）。",
      "to need": "to need 是不定詞，放在這裡句子不成立。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-cloze-meaning-grammar"],
     "feedback": "主詞 'A plant' 是單數，所以動詞用 needs（第三人稱單數）：A plant needs water——語意（需要水才能活）和語法都對。"},

    {"question_id": "R9-cloze-2", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "空格 (2)：'...because sunlight ___ them make their food.' 最適合填入哪個字？", "answer": "helps",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cloze"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.cloze"],
     "options": ["helps", "help", "helping", "helped"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "help": "主詞 sunlight 是單數，要用 helps；help 用於複數主詞。",
      "helping": "helping 是 -ing 形，不能單獨當主要動詞。",
      "helped": "helped 是過去式，但整段用現在式（comes、stay、need），時態要一致，所以用 helps。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-cloze-meaning-grammar"],
     "feedback": "主詞 sunlight 單數且整段是現在式，所以用 helps：sunlight helps them make their food——主詞一致＋時態一致。"},

    {"question_id": "R9-gap-3", "type": "mcq", "validation_method": "expert",
     "stem": "空格 (3)：下列哪一句最適合填入，讓整段讀起來通順又不離題？", "answer": "Good soil holds the roots and gives the plant food.（好的土壤抓住根，並供給植物養分）",
     "kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.gap-filling"], "required_kp_ids": ["eng.t_adv.reading.gap-filling"],
     "options": ["Good soil holds the roots and gives the plant food.（好的土壤抓住根，並供給植物養分）", "Many animals sleep during the day.（許多動物白天睡覺）", "Flowers come in many beautiful colors.（花有很多美麗的顏色）", "Too much water is always bad for every plant.（太多水對每種植物都一定有害）"],
     "distractor_rationales": {
      "Many animals sleep during the day.（許多動物白天睡覺）": "這跳到動物的主題，和前後講『植物需要的東西』離題。",
      "Flowers come in many beautiful colors.（花有很多美麗的顏色）": "這講花的顏色，和空格前句『土壤要好』接不上，也離題。",
      "Too much water is always bad for every plant.（太多水對每種植物都一定有害）": "這和前文『植物需要水』的語氣相反，而且用 always 太絕對，不合文意。"},
     "answer_evidence": ["c-gap-filling-sentence"],
     "feedback": "空格前一句說『土壤必須好』，後一句說『有了水、陽光和好土壤，植物就能長得好』——所以中間要接一句解釋好土壤的作用：Good soil holds the roots and gives the plant food。前後銜接自然、主題一致。"}
   ],

   "selfeval": ["還不熟", "快會了", "會了"],
   "selfeval_note": "翻看答案自己判斷（不自動判讀）；選完進入 SRS 間隔複習。",

   "shadowing": {
    "note": "朗讀練習（不產音檔、不自動判讀）：出聲把填好的句子讀通順，一邊讀一邊確認『字的形式對不對（needs／helps）』『句子接起來順不順』。",
    "lines": [
     {"text": "A plant needs water every day to stay alive."},
     {"text": "Good soil holds the roots and gives the plant food."}
    ]
   }
  }
 ]
}
